The developer ﬁnds that the easiest way to ﬁx the code is to eliminate the variable
d, so the counting of the sum of a+b will be done “on the ﬂy.”The corrected code
looks as follows:
intmain( intargc, _TCHAR* argv[])
{
short a,b,c;
scanf("%d",&a);scanf("%d",&b);
scanf("%d",&c);
if(abs(a-b)<c && c<a+b)
printf ("yes");
else
printf("no");
return 0;
}
The developer checks the test again for a =b=c=16,500, and now, the
program works correctly.

